# Claude Code's per-repo working directory. The transient things in it are
# `worktrees/` -- git worktrees nested inside the repo itself, one per parallel
# session, each a full checkout with its own `.git` file.
# Untracked, they show
# up as a permanent `?? .claude/` in every `git status` and are one `git add -A`
# away from being swept in.
#
# SCOPED TO THE TRANSIENT PARTS, not to `.claude/` wholesale, deliberately:
# `.claude/settings.json`, `.claude/agents/`, `.claude/skills/` and
# `.claude/workflows/` are shared project configuration that a team may well WANT
# tracked and a
# blanket `.claude/` would have silently ignored them. What is
# ignored here is what is machine-local by nature -- a worktree belongs to one
# checkout on one host, and `settings.local.json` is per-user by Claude Code's
# own convention.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local secrets. No example is tracked: tests/sweep/tree.test.ts would refuse one as a dot path.
.env
.env.*

# Superpowers SDD scratch: ledger, task briefs, implementer reports and review
# packages for a plan being executed. Machine-local and per-run by nature, and
# regenerated from the plan file, so it is never worth tracking. Same reasoning
# as `.claude/worktrees/` above -- untracked it would sit in every `git status`
# one `git add -A` away from being swept into a commit.
.superpowers/

# Build output, dependencies and tool caches.
node_modules/
/dist/
.astro/
.wrangler/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.lighthouse/
tools/screenshots/out/

# Wrangler's local secrets. Never commit a real one; see README "Local development".
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Security-sweep run directories (Task 18): per-run, machine-local, regenerated by each run.
.claude/security-sweeps/

# A safety net only: raw design files never sit inside the repository, and ingest refuses a
# --dir folder inside the repository (Ruling 99), design/incoming/ included. A folder the person
# extracts, or the files an agent saves from an artifact, go outside it (design/README.md); this
# line keeps a stray copy from ever being committed.
design/incoming/
